Development started with setting up a Git repository and a virtual environment, followed by building the database and connecting it to the backend. The face capture, encoding, and matching features were then implemented, along with attendance logic that prevents duplicate entries for the same student in one session. After this, the dashboard, report generation, login system, and role-based access were developed. The code was organized into separate folders for models, templates, static files, the face module, the database, and tests, which kept the project clean and maintainable. The team followed an agile approach, first building a minimum working version and then adding extra features, committing code daily with clear messages so that progress was always traceable.
